  <static seed="2114" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/FractionPercentDecimal/FractionToDecimal70.pg">
    <statement><p>Write the mixed number as a decimal number.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>{3{\textstyle\frac{3}{4}}}</m> = <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>{6{\textstyle\frac{3}{8}}}</m> = <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3.75</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6.375</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>To change a fraction to decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator. We can simply copy over the integer part of a mixed number.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>{3{\textstyle\frac{3}{4}}} = 3 + 3 \div 4 = 3.75</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>{6{\textstyle\frac{3}{8}}} = 6 + 3 \div 8 = 6.375</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</solution>
